1
00:00:04,350 --> 00:00:07,500
Hundreds of traders are active on Strike every day,

2
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:13,840
but there's no way for them to talk to each other. Strike tam-tam fixes that, on-chain.

3
00:00:15,080 --> 00:00:21,180
I connect my Cardano wallet. Strike tam-tam finds my Strike account and shows my stats.

4
00:00:21,480 --> 00:00:24,590
No sign-up: the wallet is the identity.

5
00:00:25,380 --> 00:00:30,170
I find a trader by nickname or ADA Handle, straight from Strike's leaderboard,

6
00:00:30,470 --> 00:00:35,270
and the preview shows exactly the NFT they'll receive, with my sender mark.

7
00:00:36,080 --> 00:00:39,130
One signature, about one and a half ADA,

8
00:00:39,430 --> 00:00:41,780
and the message lands in their wallet.

9
00:00:45,580 --> 00:00:49,190
One message can also go to up to ten traders at once.

10
00:00:53,080 --> 00:00:56,840
Each of them gets their own NFT, two per transaction.

11
00:01:03,080 --> 00:01:05,700
Each transaction is signed in the wallet,

12
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:08,930
and every recipient gets a link to their message.

13
00:01:18,580 --> 00:01:23,040
The inbox shows who's writing, with their Strike stats and the full NFT,

14
00:01:23,340 --> 00:01:26,870
and one click opens it in full size on pool.pm.

15
00:01:32,580 --> 00:01:36,960
Encrypted messages unlock with the passphrase, right in the inbox.

16
00:01:37,260 --> 00:01:40,480
On-chain, only a placeholder is readable.

17
00:01:41,280 --> 00:01:45,240
Strike tam-tam: every trader, one message away.
